WEBVTT

00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:30.436
And there definitely wasn't
willingness or openness to the idea

00:04:30.476 --> 00:04:32.556
that corporate America
wasn't a meritocracy.

00:04:32.556 --> 00:04:34.956
And that shows up differently
for different people.

00:04:34.996 --> 00:04:37.236
And it's such an important
conversation to have,

00:04:37.236 --> 00:04:38.436
because without it,

00:04:38.436 --> 00:04:41.716
I think certain groups are told
to just keep working harder and harder

00:04:41.756 --> 00:04:45.676
and yet not really able to understand
or even talk about the fact

00:04:45.716 --> 00:04:48.116
that the system does treat
some of us differently,

00:04:48.116 --> 00:04:50.916
and we need to talk about that
if we're going to change it.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:54.076
So that's one big concept:
corporate America is not a meritocracy.

00:04:54.076 --> 00:04:57.396
The second concept I want to talk about
is that we all can have power,

00:04:57.436 --> 00:04:59.076
we are all powerful.

00:04:59.076 --> 00:05:02.436
And I believe we find power
through the idea of me